<title>JAPAN: Indonesia cuts February Minas to $21.36/bbl.</title>
<headline>Indonesia cuts February Minas to $21.36/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The price of Indonesia's main Minas crude oil for February lifting was calculated at $21.36 per barrel, down $2.77 from January, traders said on Friday.  </p>
<p>Prices of other grades are as follows:</p>
<p>    TYPE		  FEB	     JAN</p>
<p> Ardjuna		  21.50	   24.10</p>
<p> Arun Condensate	21.25	   23.83</p>
<p> Attaka		   22.25	   24.91</p>
<p> Cinta		    20.65	   23.35</p>
<p> Duri		     19.80	   22.47</p>
<p> Handil		   21.13	   23.76</p>
<p> Lalang		   21.16	   23.85</p>
<p> Widuri		   20.54	   23.28</p>
<p> Belida		   22.36	   24.99</p>
<p> Anoa		     22.65	   25.31</p>
<p> Badak		    22.25	   24.91</p>
<p> Bekapai		  22.25	   24.91</p>
<p> Bunyu		    21.06	   23.83</p>
<p> Jatibarang	     20.35	   23.12</p>
<p> Bontang Mix	    21.05	   23.63</p>
<p> Walio		    21.16	   23.93</p>
<p>--Tokyo Energy Desk +81-3-5473-3708</p>
